# Redoubt isolation-eme.patch  (Android, android.txt)
# Owner: LW-M7-39. Redoubt Gecko/GeckoView change for Firefox 158; drop at the
# 159 rebase (upstream bugs 2067689 and 2075686 do the same there, see below).
#
# Owner decision 2026-10-15, verbatim: "lets analyse this in more detail and
# try to fix" (the DRM crash under isolation found in LW-M7-51).
#
# The defect (Firefox 158 + 158.0-2's isolated content, Android 12+)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# With media.eme.enabled true, a page calling
# navigator.requestMediaKeySystemAccess("com.widevine.alpha", ...) makes the
# CONTENT process ask Java whether Widevine exists before the app is asked:
#   MediaKeySystemAccessManager -> MediaKeySystemAccess::GetKeySystemStatus()
#     -> java::MediaDrmProxy::IsSchemeSupported()      (geckoview-prefs.js sets
#        media.mediadrm-widevinecdm.visible=true)
#   MediaKeySystemAccess::GetSupportedConfig() -> KeySystemConfig::Supports()
#     and CreateWivineL3KeySystemConfigs() -> MediaDrmProxy.isSchemeSupported /
#     IsCryptoSchemeSupported -> android.media.MediaDrm.isCryptoSchemeSupported
# In an isolated content process (isolated_app) SELinux denies the
# IDrmFactory/widevine (and clearkey) service lookup, MediaDrm throws
# IllegalArgumentException("Failed to query crypto scheme support"), and
# because @WrapForJNI calls treat a Java exception as fatal, the Gecko thread
# dies: the tab crashes, Fenix reloads it, it crashes again (836 crashes in 7
# minutes on the API 34 emulator, docs/android/evidence/lw-m7-51/). Below
# Android 12 content is not isolated and the query works.
#
# The rest of the EME path was already process-safe in 158.0: when the Java
# decoder module is not allowed (isolated content), MediaKeys::CreateCDMProxy()
# creates the CDM in RDD (RemoteMediaManagerChild::CreateCDM ->
# RemoteCDMProxy -> MediaDrmRemoteCDMParent, NDK AMediaDrm/AMediaCrypto), and
# encrypted H.264/AAC are decrypted and decoded together there by the MediaCodec
# NDK through ffvpx (FFmpegDataDecoder::MaybeAttachCDM). RDD runs as
# untrusted_app and may use the DRM HAL. Only the support QUERY was left in
# content. Upstream moves it to the parent in Firefox 159 (bug 2067689, five
# parts, ~1000 lines, gfxVars + an AndroidDecoderModule rewrite that conflicts
# with isolation-media-codecs-in-content.patch); this patch does the same with
# the smallest change that fits 158.0-2's isolation gate.
#
# What it does
# ------------
# 1. Parent, only while media.redoubt-isolation-media.enabled is true (the
#    locked gate pref, true exactly when content runs isolated: Android 12+,
#    isolation-media-prefs.patch): GeckoMediaPluginServiceParent::
#    LoadFromEnvironment(), on the GMP thread at the first content-process
#    launch, asks the NDK AMediaDrm_isCryptoSchemeSupported +
#    AMediaCrypto_isCryptoSchemeSupported for Widevine (as upstream's part 3
#    does in the same function) and publishes the answer as the locked
#    default-branch pref media.redoubt-eme.widevine-support (0 not known yet,
#    1 no, 2 yes). Prefs reach every process, isolated content included, and a
#    lock beats about:config/prefs.js. Logcat (tag Gecko):
#      Redoubt isolation-eme: parent found Widevine supported; ...
# 2. Content, gate true: KeySystemConfig::Supports() and
#    MediaKeySystemAccess::GetKeySystemStatus() read that pref instead of
#    calling MediaDrm; CreateWivineL3KeySystemConfigs() offers H.264 and AAC in
#    MP4, decrypt-and-decode (what RDD actually plays while content is
#    isolated: isolation-media-codecs-in-content.patch makes RDD refuse every
#    other decoder, CDM or not) and calls no Java. Before the parent's answer
#    arrives (0), Widevine is "not installed" and the request rejects
#    (NotSupportedError), as upstream's "Unknown" does.
#    Gate false (Android 8-11): every changed line takes 158.0's path.
# 3. MediaDrmProxy.isSchemeSupported/IsCryptoSchemeSupported (GeckoView Java):
#    a RuntimeException from MediaDrm/MediaCrypto is caught and reported as
#    "not supported" instead of killing the calling Gecko thread. Backstop on
#    every Android version; with 1+2 no isolated process calls it any more.
# 4. Backport of upstream bug 2075686 (RemoteCDMProxy, the RDD CDM proxy used
#    only for isolated content): closing a session notifies MediaKeySession
#    (keystatuseschange + "closed"), and an RDD crash closes the sessions with
#    an error instead of hitting MOZ_ASSERT_UNREACHABLE.
#      Bug 2075686 - Ensure RemoteCDMProxy closes sessions appropriately.
#      r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu; Author: Andrew Osmond
#      <aosmond@mozilla.com>, 2026-09-29; mozilla-firefox commit
#      476a668978c266e21a1302839b155cc2ebe32460 (Firefox 159). Upstream patch
#      sha256 (github.com/.../commit/<sha>.patch, fetched 2026-10-15):
#      cef6703c2adfe89bd67076d0cb3d2557ffdc3223df49efa9ecefb79cfffc84d8
#    Applied verbatim (both hunks, fuzz 0 on 158.0).
# 5. MediaDrmRemoteCDMParent::HandleExpirationUpdate (RDD, isolated content
#    only): MediaDrm reports an expiration of 0 for keys that never expire; it
#    was passed on as 0 ms, so MediaKeySession.expiration read 1 January 1970
#    and a player that honours it (Shaka) closed the session right after the
#    license: with item 4 the keys go with it and playback stalls when the
#    buffer runs out (measured on the API 34 emulator: Widevine stream stopped
#    at 7.9 s, "waitingforkey"). 0 now becomes NaN, EME's "no expiration", as
#    the Java path (which never reports one) and the spec have it. Upstream
#    main has the same code (not reported upstream; owner rule).
# 6. MediaDrmRemoteCDMParent::RecvInit (RDD, isolated content only): Init, and
#    with it createMediaKeys(), resolved before the AMediaCrypto existed. On the
#    first use of an origin the crypto session waits for provisioning, and a
#    decoder created in that window could not attach the CDM, fell back to a
#    software decoder ffvpx does not have and failed ("unable to find codec";
#    measured: 2 of 9 first plays on a fresh profile). Init now resolves once
#    the crypto exists, or rejects with its error. And a failed provisioning,
#    which is sticky, no longer makes EnsureHasAMediaCrypto() retry forever.
#    Upstream main has the same code.
# 7. MediaDrmRemoteCDMParent::RecvUpdateSession (RDD, Android 12 and 13
#    only, runtime check): Widevine in privacy mode first asks the page for
#    its service certificate (message 0804). After the page's response
#    (SignedMessage type 5) the CDM signals EVENT_KEY_REQUIRED with EMPTY
#    data, and HandleEvent() makes the real license request. The Android 12
#    and 13 NDK drops events with empty data (AOSP frameworks/av
#    media/ndk/NdkMediaDrm.cpp DrmListener::sendEvent "if (dataSize > 0)",
#    logcat "E NdkMediaDrm: invalid event data size=0"; Android 14 has
#    ">= 0"), so no license was requested and every Widevine play stopped at
#    ~8 s ("waitingforkey"; 158.0-3 acceptance, API 31). There the CDM now
#    calls HandleEvent(EVENT_KEY_REQUIRED, empty data) itself right after a
#    service certificate response, which is what the event does on Android
#    14. If the event arrives anyway, HandleEventCb() skips it once, so a
#    session still makes exactly one license request. Android 14+ and the
#    Java path (Android 8-11, not isolated) are unchanged. Not covered: a
#    license RENEWAL is also signalled by an empty KEY_REQUIRED and is still
#    lost on Android 12 and 13 (keys expire instead of renewing); the other
#    empty events (provision required, key expired, vendor defined, session
#    reclaimed) are ignored by HandleEvent() on every version anyway.
#    Upstream main has the same stall on Android 12 and 13 (not reported
#    upstream; owner rule).
#
# Whether DRM is ON is not decided here: media.eme.enabled and the app's
# DRM-controlled content permission decide (drm-permission-default.patch,
# settings/android.cfg). This patch only makes the query safe and correct in
# isolated content, so that the switch can work on Android 12+ too.
#
# Security: no new process and no new IPC protocol. The Widevine query runs in
# the parent (untrusted_app, already the HAL's client for everything else);
# license messages and encrypted samples go content -> RDD over the PRemoteCDM
# protocol upstream 158.0 already ships, to the RDD process that already
# decodes H.264/AAC for isolated content. The DRM HAL and Widevine run in their
# own system processes, never in a Redoubt process. Isolated content still
# cannot reach the HAL; it only reads a locked integer.
#
# Upstream files touched
# ----------------------
#   dom/media/eme/KeySystemConfig.cpp         Supports(), CreateWivineL3KeySystemConfigs()
#   dom/media/eme/MediaKeySystemAccess.cpp    GetKeySystemStatus()
#   dom/media/eme/mediadrm/MediaDrmRemoteCDMParent.cpp  RecvInit(), EnsureHasAMediaCrypto(),
#                                                       HandleExpirationUpdate(), HandleEventCb(),
#                                                       RecvUpdateSession()
#   dom/media/eme/mediadrm/MediaDrmRemoteCDMParent.h    SessionEntry flag, helper
#   dom/media/gmp/GMPServiceParent.cpp        LoadFromEnvironment()
#   dom/media/ipc/RemoteCDMChild.cpp          (bug 2075686)
#   dom/media/ipc/RemoteCDMProxy.cpp          (bug 2075686)
#   mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/gecko/media/MediaDrmProxy.java
#   modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml  media.redoubt-eme.widevine-support
#
# Ordering: after isolation-media-codecs-in-content.patch (the new pref is
# added after that patch's media.redoubt-test.skip-content-codec-filter, and
# the gate pref read here is defined there).
#
# Line numbers are from the Firefox 158.0 tree AFTER the patches listed before
# this one in assets/patches/android.txt.
#
